  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "など, which means 'et cetera', 'and so on', is similar to and can be used in conjunction with や, but is generally used to conclude a list of examples, or samples of a potentially larger list.",
      "html": "など, which means 'et cetera', 'and so on', is similar to and can be used in conjunction with や, but is generally used to conclude a list of examples, or samples of a potentially larger list.",
      "credits_raw": "kappamaki",
      "content_sha256": "1f3085bbac74b4c3a9a88577ab40899da01dc5eef09a79dd655812594cb3b66e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "In the first example 'and such like' may be implied, but nado is often used in this way without necessarily literally meaning 'and so on', I think maybe it makes the sentence less rigidly precise.",
      "html": "In the first example 'and such like' may be implied, but nado is often used in this way without necessarily literally meaning 'and so on', I think maybe it makes the sentence less rigidly precise.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "04c8d7484224c4c225b7f12e3069d8e3e3e6101b368a5cb393f6ea16071cd743",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The second example is the standard 'list' usage. The particle 'ya' can be used in place of the commas.",
      "html": "The second example is the standard 'list' usage. The particle 'ya' can be used in place of the commas.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "9491b34dff8573f1123061b66a09c887942ec9eb14472327f8139ce9d4f3a83a",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "等、、、 is also used as english \"etc...\"",
      "html": "等、、、 is also used as english \"etc...\"",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "b5347ac4c89a11c4ddbcafaf3637aa7e5eb11b6da3a38b35d4ad51ef85cbf376",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "なんか and なんて have the same meaning but are colloquial terms. Another usage of those three is when you don't think much of something or contem something.",
      "html": "なんか and なんて have the same meaning but are colloquial terms. Another usage of those three is when you don't think much of something or contem something.",
      "credits_raw": "halx",
      "content_sha256": "1620869b9e9ef2538fa8a718e877e8360f6896ac42a89e47eea449a64abc79b0",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Ex.3218: Isnﾂｴt apple :ringo?",
      "html": "Ex.3218: Isnﾂｴt apple :ringo?",
      "credits_raw": "Futaro",
      "content_sha256": "41174e3e80184bd288ef2e6cbb95382b4f522ecfa5e34bcd060b6ce48cc4f7a5",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Apple juice is りんごジュース or アップルジュース.",
      "html": "Apple juice is りんごジュース or アップルジュース.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "65c079f8e102ba2cc026d7b084f47311c8ea757ed668e03374bb24f883fb3f5f",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I think など, like なんて, can also indicates that the speaker is shocked or outraged. I think it's the case in this sentence: かよわいものから りゃくだつなど！",
      "html": "I think など, like なんて, can also indicates that the speaker is shocked or outraged. I think it's the case in this sentence: かよわいものから りゃくだつなど！",
      "credits_raw": "mattaku",
      "content_sha256": "2adf8825ee1668012d4d1ed10cbcc5edf8c494887c8c26b03bac4ec0467f34f8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Could など be used after a series of も instead of や?. For example \"He stole money, the credit cards, a watch, and other things\". お金もクレジットカ−ドも時計も服など盗んだ",
      "html": "Could など be used after a series of も instead of や?. For example \"He stole money, the credit cards, a watch, and other things\". お金もクレジットカ−ドも時計も服など盗んだ",
      "credits_raw": "Weasker",
      "content_sha256": "93c636f562425cf86a1ccfe7e240e8c7dafef3d8b6ef2d9039919cb8d2c2a934",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "魚や豚肉などを買いました。",
      "html": "魚や豚肉などを買いました。",
      "credits_raw": "Joemel",
      "content_sha256": "b89bc9d4eefe6e3424f9bfc3b82a27251dd606d06541b46b29a2c40bd954794f",
